/* ---- MiG-29 / Su-27 ILS indication, laid out from the real SUV-29 ILS photographs and the SUV mode charts ----
   Top: indicated airspeed (left, envelope limit above it, acceleration mark below) and altitude (right; radio altitude with a "р" under 1000 m;
   the locked target's altitude above it). Heading scale between them while searching; in a lock it becomes the time-to-impact bar, anchored on the left scale.
   Left scale: range in km, launch-zone marks (Rmax flag, Rne bar, Rmin flag) and a hollow arrow at target range.
   Right scale: closure speed with a small arrow (antenna elevation while scanning).
   Centre: horizon line (wings with a centre gap while searching, one long line in a lock) with the aircraft tick; in a lock the big circle sits at the lead point
   (permitted steering error) and the small circle with a stem on the target. Left column: ППС/ЗПС hemisphere, РЛ/ТП channel, А auto, Г↑/Г↓ aspect, Ф illumination.
   Bottom: ПР launch permitted, ИЗЛ radiating, ОТВ break away, span bracket, selected missile. */
