/* ============ GROUND WAR: 2K12 Kub (SA-6) battery, ZSU-23-4 Shilka, ground targets, free-fall bombs, rockets and CCIP ============
   2K12 Kub-M3 (SA-6 'Gainful'): one 1S91 'Straight Flush' SURN radar vehicle (1S11 search radar, about 75 km; 1S31 continuous-wave
   tracker / illuminator, illumination from 28 km) and four 2P25 launchers with three 3M9 missiles each. Engagement 4-25 km, 20-8,000 m,
   system reaction 22-24 s, target speed up to about Mach 1.75 head-on. 3M9: 599 kg, solid booster whose empty case becomes a ramjet, about
   Mach 2.8, 56 kg warhead with proximity fuze, semi-active homing on the CW illumination; the seeker tracks the Doppler shift, so a target
   flying at right angles to the radar (no closing speed) drops out of the tracking gate.
   ZSU-23-4 Shilka: four 2A7 23 mm cannon, 850-1,000 rds/min per barrel, 980 m/s HE-T, 2,000 rounds, bursts of 3-10 rounds per barrel,
   effective to about 2.5 km slant and 1.5 km altitude; RPK-2 'Gun Dish' Ku-band radar sees aircraft to 20 km, ground clutter gives
   false returns below about 60 m, and automatic tracking struggles with fast crossing targets inside 7-8 km.
   Stores: Mk 82 (227 kg, 87 kg Tritonal, 273 mm) and FAB-250 M-62 (250 kg, 100 kg HE, 300 mm) free-fall bombs; LAU-10 (4 Zuni, 127 mm,
   36 kg motor, ~720 m/s, 8 km) and B-8M1 (20 S-8KOM, 11.3 kg, HEAT 400 mm penetration plus fragmentation, ~700 m/s, 1.3-4 km).
   CCIP: the impact point of the selected store is computed every frame by flying the same equations the weapon flies. */
