/* ============ DYNAMIC CAMPAIGN: a 300 km theatre, a living front, seasons, weather, an enemy air force with a plan ============
   Blue holds the south, red the north. The front is a line through twelve control points; each point has a battalion's worth of
   tanks, IFVs and infantry per side that hold, advance and fight with the ones across the line. Three sectors are "hot" at any time
   (two red offensives, one blue), and the front moves where one side out-fights the other. Red runs CAP stations, scrambles
   interceptors at anything that crosses into its airspace, and sends bomb-carrying strikes at our troops and our airfields.
   A base is lost when the front rolls over it. The calendar moves ten days per campaign day, so the seasons turn: snow line,
   field colours, winter cover, the sun's path and the weather all follow it. One host runs the war; friends join and fly in it. */
const CMP_SZ=300000;
