/* ============ v121: air-to-ground radar modes, deeper targeting pods, the Maverick family, F-4 Mavericks ============
   A/G radar (all A/G-capable jets, shown automatically in A/G master mode):
     GM / RBM  real-beam ground map: terrain returns by slope and radar shadow, cultural returns, painted as the antenna sweeps and fading afterglow
     EXP       Doppler-beam-sharpened patch around the cursor (4x / 8x / 16x by jet), cannot be built on the nose (DBS blind sector)
     GMT       moving-target indication: only things that move and are not beaming show up, with ground speed and heading
     SEA       sea clutter and ships; land is suppressed
     AGR       air-to-ground ranging: precise slant range to the cursor point, slaves the pod / Maverick view
   PgUp / PgDn = next / previous mode, Insert = radar cursor to SPI, Delete = EXP level or freeze.
   Targeting pods: LITENING, SNIPER XR, ATFLIR, LANTIRN with their own field-of-view steps, CCD-TV / FLIR WHOT / BHOT video, gain and level,
   laser code and auto-lase time, laser range, point-track with coast, field-of-regard indicator and range source (LRF / AGR / INS).
   Mavericks: A and B (early TV, contrast tracker, day only), H (CCD, works into dusk), D / G (IIR), E (laser), F (Navy IIR). Lock range depends on
   target contrast or heat, daylight, weather and magnification. F-4E carries A / B / D / G / H on a LAU-88 on stations 2 and 8. */
